Let $n\geq1$ and $t\geq1$. Let $u$ be the largest $t$-dense divisor
of $n$, and put $v=n/u$. Then $\gcd(u,v)=1$, and every prime divisor
of $v$ exceeds $t u$. Each maximal $t$-dense block of $\Div(n)$ is a
disjoint union of sets
\begin{equation}
 b\Div(u)=\{ba:a\mid u\},\qquad b\mid v.
\end{equation}
Consequently,
\begin{equation}
 \tau(u)\mid T_t(n,k),\qquad
 T_t(n,1)=T_t(n,r)=\min_k T_t(n,k)=\tau(u).
\end{equation}
